{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Data Bits}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Data_Bits}
\pard \b Data Bits\plain\fs24 
\par An RS232 comm port setting which determines how many bits make up a single character.
\par 
\par It is important that the same value is selected within Remcon32 as in the program running on the remote PC.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Dial a phone number}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 7HBQVE}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Close Port}
\b Dial a phone number\plain\fs24 
\par Allows a connection to be made to a remote PC via a modem connected to the comms port.
\par 
\par When selected a dialog will appear requesting the phone number to be dialed.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm2.wmf\}
\par 
\par This function is only available when the comms port is \uldb open\plain\fs24 {\v 7HMXZG}.
\par 
\par Use of modem communication is likely to require \i Xon/RTS \plain\fs24 to be selected in the \uldb flow control\plain\fs24 {\v Flow_Control} settings.
\par 
\par To make the program ready for dialing in from a remote PC, it is necessary to open the comms port which has the modem connected to it.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Echo}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} IC2YSC}
\pard \b Echo\plain\fs24 
\par Controls whether characters returned by the SEM are displayed in the text window.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Flow Control}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Flow_Control}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} COM port SELECTION}
\b Flow Control\plain\fs24 
\par An RS232 comm port setting which determines how data overrun is prevented.
\par 
\par It is important that the same value is selected within Remcon32 as in the program running on the remote PC.
\par 
\par For remote communications via a modem \i Xon/RTS\plain\fs24  is likely to be required.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} General Description}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} General_Description}
\pard\keepn \fs36 General Description
\par \pard \fs24 Remcon32 is a utility program which permits a remote PC to communicate with the SEM using an RS232 protocol.
\par 
\par Details of the RS232 protocol are published by LEO under the \b OpenX\plain\fs24  policy. Contact your local LEO representative for further details.
\par 
\par Remcon32 has several advanced features designed to enhance its usefulness, namely :
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 1.\tab Remote PC connection via a \uldb modem\plain\fs24 {\v 7HBQVE}.
\par 2.\tab Logging a remote control session to a \uldb text file\plain\fs24 {\v 4_C4CL}
\par 3.\tab \uldb Local mode\plain\fs24 {\v 1UKN0RR} operation for testing remote control sequences
\par 4.\tab Easy configuration of \uldb comm port settings\plain\fs24 {\v 1VDW3L3}
\par 
\par See also
\par \uldb Multiple Instances\plain\fs24 {\v Multiple_Instances_of_RemCon32}
\par \uldb Auto Start in SEM user Interface\plain\fs24 {\v Auto_Start_of_RemCon32_when_logging_on_to_the_SEM_User_Interface}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Hang up}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Hang_up}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Comms Settings}
\b Hang up\plain\fs24 
\par Disconnects a remote session via a modem.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Keep On Top}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} JH.OWC}
\pard \b Keep On Top\plain\fs24 
\par Selected to ensure that the Remcon32 window will always be uppermost of the windows on display.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Local Mode}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 1UKN0RR}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Contents}
\fs36 Local Mode
\par \fs24 Allows RS232 commands to be tried locally to the SEM by typing the relevant character sequence in the text window.
\par 
\par This mode is useful for checking that the SEM is responding correctly to RS232 commands and for trying out sequences of commands before coding them into an automated control program.
\par 
\par This mode will normally be used with\ul  Echo On\plain\fs24 {\v IC2YSC} selected.
\par 
\par When this mode is selected no output is sent to the comms port.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} On Startup}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} On_Startup}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Data Bits}
\b On Startup\plain\fs24 
\par Used to determine the actions taken when the program is started.
\par 
\par If the box is checked the comms port will be opened and the program will be minimised, putting it into the ready state to receive external RS232 commands.
\par 
\par If the box is not checked then the port will need to be opened manually.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Open Log File}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 4_C4CL}
\pard \fs36 Open Log File
\par \fs24 Displays a file selection dialog to allow a filename to be selected so that all RS232 commands and responses can be recorded in a file.
\par 
\par Commands will be logged from when a file is selected until the file is \uldb closed\plain\fs24 {\v 1IQ5_DN}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Open Port}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 7HMXZG}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Dial a phone number}
\b Open Port\plain\fs24 
\par Initialises the RS232 port ready for communications.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Parity}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Parity}
\pard \b Parity\plain\fs24 
\par An RS232 comm port setting which determines how error checking is performed on the data.
\par 
\par The default value for this setting is \i None.\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par It is important that the same value is selected within Remcon32 as in the program running on the remote PC.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Properties}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 11MZUNO}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Echo}
\b Properties\plain\fs24 
\par This collection of comms properties are used for diagnostic purposes and their settings should not be changed.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stop Bits}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stop_Bits}
\pard \b Stop Bits\plain\fs24 
\par An RS232 comm port setting which determines how many bits are used to terminate a transmission.
\par 
\par It is important that the same value is selected within Remcon32 as in the program running on the remote PC.
\par \page
