\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \ul Local Mode\plain\fs24 {\v 1UKN0RR}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Transmit text file}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} A_KU2W}
\pard\tx355 \b Transmit text file\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 Allows a file on disk to be transmitted to the remote PC via the RS232 connection.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 When activated a standard file selection dialog allows the relevant file to be selected.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 This function is only enabled when the comms port is \uldb open\plain\fs24 {\v 7HMXZG}.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Multiple Instances of RemCon32}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Multiple_Instances_of_RemCon32}
\pard\keepn \fs36 Multiple Instances of RemCon32
\par \pard \fs24 If you wish to use multiple instances of RemCon32 it is necessary to identify which settings apply to which instance of RemCon32.
\par This is achieved by adding a command line argument (alphanumeric characters only) which identifies the group of settings to be used.
\par 
\par e.g. ..\'5cleo\'5cleo32\'5cRemCon32.exe EDX
\par 
\par The identifier is displayed in the RemCon32 Caption
\par \page
